# Pinned dependency versions for CI and Docker builds.
# See engdocs/archive/designs/image-dependency-versioning.md for the versioning
# strategy (archived, but still the only written record of it).
#
# Update these when bumping automation/image pins. The internal/deps package
# defines minimum compatible versions (may lag behind these pins).

DOLT_VERSION=2.2.0
BD_REPO=gastownhall/beads
# BD_VERSION is the installable default: a PUBLISHED beads release whose tarball
# SHA is pinned in .github/scripts/install-bd-archive.sh. Every required CI job
# downloads exactly this tarball, so it can only ever name a tag that has a
# GitHub Release with all four os/arch assets.
#
# It was held at v1.1.0 because no published release carried the conditional-write
# flags `--if-assignee`/`--if-status` (a rejected precondition is exit 13, nothing
# written, which is where the exit-13 constant comes from). That constraint is
# now lifted: v1.3.0 was cut from beads main well past 6e8af8bf8 (beads#5008,
# 2026-07-24) and 4b1d9c875 (beads#5364, 2026-08-05), and v1.3.1 (the
# release/1.3.0 hotfix line) keeps them and publishes tarballs for all four
# os/arch tuples, so the ReleaseIfCurrent CAS contract now runs on
# the installable default rather than only on the source-built cell below.
BD_VERSION=v1.3.1
BR_VERSION=0.1.20

# Cross-version contract-test matrix pins.
# See engdocs/design/beads-gascity-contract-test-system.md.
# BD_PREV_VERSION is the minimum-supported bd: a published release whose tarball
# SHA is pinned in .github/scripts/install-bd-archive.sh (no API fallback on the
# required path). BD_CURRENT_VERSION is the bleeding-edge cell at BD_CURRENT_REF
# (a gastownhall/beads commit). Bump BD_CURRENT_REF deliberately, in lockstep
# with the vendored corpus, per the coordination protocol. Under Bazel the prev
# cell runs BD_PREV_VERSION's release archive (MODULE.bazel bd_bin_v*), and the
# current cell, like every other test that runs a real bd, runs //tools/bd:bd,
# which Bazel builds from the beads commit go.mod pins (BD_CURRENT_REF);
# scripts/bd_contract_pins_test.go keeps both on these pins. Normally
# BD_CURRENT_REF is BD_CURRENT_VERSION's tag commit.
#
# The matrix axis is BD_PREV_VERSION vs BD_CURRENT_VERSION -- v1.0.4 against
# v1.3.1 -- and BD_VERSION is not a cell in it, so the installable default
# is free to sit anywhere at or above the floor without narrowing the axis.
#
# TEMPORARY: BD_CURRENT_REF is NOT a tag commit right now. It is a beads main
# commit (the S6b/S6c/S6d merge, gastownhall/beads#7471), pinned in go.mod as
# the pseudo-version v1.3.1-0.20261010181156-c4e667cb14c3, because the native
# HTTP backend needs beads' S6 series and no beads release carries it yet.
# beads cuts releases on release branches, so v1.3.1 is not an ancestor of main
# and that pseudo-version sorts BELOW v1.3.1 even though main's code is newer.
# Until the next beads release: go.mod, BD_CURRENT_REF, //tools/bd:bd and the
# agent image's source build name that main commit, while BD_CURRENT_VERSION
# and the installable default (BD_VERSION, the tarball the go-test jobs
# install) stay on the published v1.3.1, whose schema is older than the one gc
# links. Move all of them back onto one release tag when beads cuts it. Until
# then the Tier A acceptance suite, run by go test against that tarball,
# panics in TestMain's RequireBdSchemaParity check, so a go-test lane has to
# build bd at BD_CURRENT_REF with CGO, as nightly.yml does. Mac Regression's
# Tier A and RC Gate's acceptance A still install the tarball.
#
# BD_CURRENT_SOURCE_VERSION is the version string the source at BD_CURRENT_REF
# declares (cmd/bd/version.go `Version = "..."`). The agent image and
# //tools/bd:bd build bd from that source and stamp exactly this version
# (contrib/k8s/Dockerfile.agent BD_VERSION, whose grep fails the build on drift;
# tools/bd/BUILD.bazel x_defs, held to it by scripts/bd_contract_pins_test.go),
# so it is what that bd reports. It equals BD_CURRENT_VERSION when
# BD_CURRENT_REF is a tag commit (scripts/bd_version_pin_test.go enforces that);
# for the main pin above it is v1.3.0, because beads main still declares 1.3.0
# (the 1.3.1 bump exists only on the release branch). Every gc bd version floor
# must be at or below it, so no runtime gate refuses the pinned bd (also
# enforced there).
#
# BD_PREV_VERSION is also the floor that keeps BdStore's raw-SQL release fallback
# alive (bdSQLStringLiteral, releaseIfCurrentViaEmbeddedDoltSQL,
# parseDoltRowsAffected, isBdSQLUnsupportedInEmbeddedMode). Raising it past
# beads#5008 would delete all four, so it stays where it is: this bump is a pin
# move, not a support-floor decision.
BD_PREV_VERSION=v1.0.4
BD_CURRENT_VERSION=v1.3.1
BD_CURRENT_REF=c4e667cb14c3c29a420005e0ec029a0882c6ebc3
BD_CURRENT_SOURCE_VERSION=v1.3.0
